From 6c3c9aae13dd616938a66121d544b96c7181d963 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthuchamy Kumar <muthucha@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 19:38:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] patch: agent-side DPP per-BSS connector/csign IPC via
 cACTION_APMANAGER_WIFI_CREDENTIALS_UPDATE_REQUEST

Carry DPP connector/csign (per BSS) and netaccesskey (Agent-wide) from
son_slave to ap_manager over the existing WIFI_CREDENTIALS_UPDATE_REQUEST
IPC message instead of the WSC M2 wire format:

- beerocks_message_apmanager.yaml/.h/.cpp: new cDppBssCredentials class
  (bssid + variable-length connector/csign) and dpp_bss_credentials/
  dpp_netaccesskey sibling fields on
  cACTION_APMANAGER_WIFI_CREDENTIALS_UPDATE_REQUEST.
- ap_autoconfiguration_task.cpp/.h: builds cDppBssCredentials per BSS and
  writes the single Agent-wide netaccesskey from
  AgentDB::dpp_credentials.nak_private_der when sending the message.
- ap_manager.cpp: reads dpp_bss_credentials by BSSID and the Agent-wide
  netaccesskey, populating sBssInfoConf for the HAL layer.
- ap_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp / dwpal / dwpald / whm / sta_wlan_hal_nl80211.cpp,
  son_wireless_utils.h/.cpp, dpp_configurator_task.cpp, dpp_agent_task.h/.cpp,
  bpl_cfg_wifi.cpp, eWscAuth.yaml/.h: DPP-only auth fix (RSN-protected
  instead of open), AKM-combo wpa_key_mgmt composition (dpp+sae,
  dpp+psk+sae, etc.), WSC_AUTH_DPP enum bit, and hostapd.conf writes for
  the DPP connector/csign/netaccesskey.

Fix two runtime issues found on hardware and add UCI persistence:

- ap_autoconfiguration_task.cpp: TLVF enforces a single monotonically
  increasing allocation-order counter across all variable-length list
  fields on a message, in YAML declaration order. Interleaving
  wifi_credentials and dpp_bss_credentials entries per-BSS therefore
  aborted with "Can't create new element before adding the previous
  one" and, once partially fixed, "Out of order allocation for
  variable length list wifi_credentials, abort!". Restructured
  send_ap_bss_configuration_message() into two fully sequential passes
  over the BSS list: all wifi_credentials entries are created and
  committed first, then all dpp_bss_credentials entries in a second
  pass, matching the field's declaration order on the message.
- framework/platform/bpl/cfg/uci/bpl_cfg_wifi.cpp: hostapd.conf was
  correctly written but UCI was never updated with the DPP connector/
  csign/netaccesskey, so the values didn't survive a UCI-driven
  hostapd.conf regeneration or reboot. Persist
  dpp_connector/dpp_csign/dpp_netaccesskey (hex-encoded DER for
  csign/netaccesskey via the existing string_utils::bytes_to_hex_string()
  helper) in both the non-MLD and MLD option-map code paths, and add the
  three keys to both cred_keys[] change-detection arrays so a value
  change actually triggers a UCI commit. Only the uci backend is
  touched; dm/linux/rdk backends are intentionally left alone.

Remove temporary DPP DEBUG tracing added while diagnosing the two
runtime issues above: work() and drain_pending_bss_config_send() no
longer log routine early returns or per-call tracing. Kept as
LOG(ERROR) since they indicate real bugs if ever hit: the order/map
mismatch guards in drain_pending_bss_config_send() and the existing
send-failure log.
